## ⚠️ PART 5 — Risk Identification & Tracking

### 5.1 — Error Handling Pattern Analysis

```
SCAN FOR ERROR HANDLING SIGNALS:

  Typed Error / Result Objects:
    Custom Result<T> / ValidationResult / Either<E,T> classes
    → Indicates structured error accumulation vs exception-throwing

  Exception Hierarchy:
    Custom exception classes extending RuntimeException / Exception
    → Capture: class names, hierarchy depth, HTTP status mappings

  Global Exception Handling:
    @ControllerAdvice / @RestControllerAdvice classes
    @ExceptionHandler methods
    ProblemDetail / RFC 7807 error response format
    → Capture: which exceptions are handled, what HTTP status returned

  Controller-Level Handling:
    try-catch blocks directly in controller methods
    → Note: indicates lack of centralized handling if present

  Severity / Level Classification:
    Enum with severity levels (INFO, WARN, ERROR, FATAL, etc.)
    → Capture: enum class name, level names and ordinal values

  Fail-Fast vs Accumulating Pattern:
    Fail-fast: stops validation at first error
    Accumulating: collects all errors before returning
    → Detect from: composite validator logic, result list accumulation

  Silent Failure Detection:
    catch(Exception e) { log.warn(...); } with no rethrow → flag as risk
    Empty catch blocks → flag as CRITICAL risk

  HTTP Status Mapping:
    @ResponseStatus annotations on exception classes
    ResponseEntity with explicit status in @ExceptionHandler
    → Map: ExceptionClass → HTTP status code
```

