## 🔎 PART 8 — Governance Gap Analysis

### 8.1 — Gap Detection Rules

```
DERIVE ALL GAPS FROM EVIDENCE. NEVER INVENT A GAP.

GAP CATEGORY 1: OBSERVABILITY GAPS
  ⛔ Health probes disabled in any environment → CRITICAL
  ⛔ No liveness probe → CRITICAL (K8s cannot restart unhealthy pod)
  ⛔ No readiness probe → HIGH (traffic sent to unready pod)
  ⚠️ No metrics instrumentation → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No distributed tracing → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No structured JSON logging → MEDIUM

GAP CATEGORY 2: SECURITY GOVERNANCE GAPS
  ⛔ No dependency vulnerability scan in pipeline → HIGH
  ⛔ CORS set to "*" without documented justification → HIGH
  ⛔ Pod security context absent → HIGH
  ⛔ No secret management (secrets in source) → CRITICAL
  ⚠️ No SAST tool in pipeline → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No network policy → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ Container running as root (no runAsNonRoot) → HIGH

GAP CATEGORY 3: GOVERNANCE STRUCTURE GAPS
  ⛔ No CODEOWNERS / MAINTAINERS file → MEDIUM
  ⛔ No architecture review process (no ADRs) → MEDIUM
  ⛔ No deployment approval gate for production → HIGH
  ⚠️ No PR template → LOW
  ⚠️ No change log → LOW

GAP CATEGORY 4: COMPLIANCE GAPS
  ⛔ No API contract / OpenAPI spec → MEDIUM
  ⛔ No code quality enforcement in pipeline → MEDIUM
  ⛔ Regulatory validator present but not tested → HIGH
  ⚠️ Error codes with no i18n message (NOT_MAPPED) → LOW
  ⚠️ No audit trail for state-changing operations → MEDIUM

GAP CATEGORY 5: RESILIENCE GAPS
  ⛔ External HTTP calls with no timeout config → HIGH
  ⛔ External HTTP calls with no circuit breaker → MEDIUM
  ⛔ Message consumer with no dead-letter queue → HIGH
  ⚠️ Cache with no TTL / eviction policy → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No graceful shutdown config → MEDIUM

GAP CATEGORY 6: DOCUMENTATION GAPS
  ⛔ No README or README under 100 words → MEDIUM
  ⛔ No API documentation (OpenAPI / Swagger) → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No runbook or operational documentation → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No CHANGELOG → LOW
  ⚠️ Public API methods without Javadoc/docstring → LOW

GAP CATEGORY 7: INFRASTRUCTURE HYGIENE
  ⛔ No resource limits on containers → HIGH
  ⛔ HPA not enabled in production → MEDIUM
  ⛔ No pod disruption budget → LOW
  ⚠️ Environment parity violations (feature in prod only) → MEDIUM
  ⚠️ No container image vulnerability scan → HIGH
```

